// ===== ACC WALL-BUYS (user 2026-06-24) — chalk outline + flush wall placement =====
// FIXED 2026-06-24: the prior pass (a) skipped chalk on a FALSE "shaders won't compile" claim
// and (b) left the gun floating ~15-17u off the wall (model sat at the trigger origin, z50).
// Now each wall-buy is the PROVEN early recipe (commit 0044a16, the t7_zm_chalk_buy_icr1 build
// that worked flawlessly): an inline chalk mesh on the wall face (see "ACC WALL-BUY CHALK
// OUTLINES" in worldspawn) + a weapon_upgrade trigger + a model struct, all co-located ON the
// wall face (2u proud) facing the room. Facing convention (verified vs the early ICR/Bowie wall-
// buys AND the stock t6_olympia prefab): model angles "0 0 0" => faces +y (room north);
// "0 180 0" => faces -y (room south). The HINT TEXT shown + the weapon/nade GIVEN come from
// "zombie_weapon_upgrade" (t6_fiveseven / t6_olympia / frag_grenade / t9_ak47) + the weapons CSV
// (500/500/100/1500) — NOT the chalk material, so a generic chalk outline is fine (user 2026-06-24).
// CHALK ONLY (user 2026-06-24): the model struct below is kept (it's the trigger's target for the
// stock pipeline) but NOTHING renders it — script_structs don't draw their model KVP, and the
// redundant 3D-gun spawn (spawn_acc_wallbuy_models) is DISABLED, so each spot shows only the chalk.
// Kept past box-only remove_all_wallbuys() by its whitelist.
